xg6frx5 xw872ko xhgbb2x xynf4tj xdjs2zz x1r9ni5o xvsnedh x1g7kj8l xqo1zpi x2qsnth xh2ebzn xx38sju x1s928wv x1m1drc7 x1unh1gc x1xrz1ek x1iygr5g x2q1x1w x1j6awrg" style="--x-height: 48px; --x-width: 48px;"><img draggable="false" height="48" width="48" class="xl1xv1r x1c9tyrk xeusxvb x1pahc9y x1ertn4p x1lliihq" alt="" aria-hidden="true" referrerpolicy="origin-when-cross-origin" src="./ganeshvideo_files/file(15).enc"></div></div></div></div><div class="x78zum5 xdl72j9 xdt5ytf x1iyjqo2 xl56j7k xeuugli x1n1b19v"><div role="gridcell" aria-colindex="2" class="x6s0dn4 x78zum5 xggjnk3 x1yc453h"><div class="x14ug900 x78zum5 x1iyjqo2 x1jchvi3 xdod15v x6ikm8r x10wlt62 x1mzt3pk x1yc453h xo1l8bm" data-testid="cell-frame-title"><span dir="auto" title="III CSE-A 2024" class="x1iyjqo2 x6ikm8r x10wlt62 x1n2onr6 xlyipyv xuxw1ft x1rg5ohu x1jchvi3 xjb2p0i xo1l8bm x17mssa0 x1ic7a3i xnpuxes" style="min-height: 0px;">III CSE-A 2024</span></div><div class="xhslqc4 x1c4vz4f x2lah0s x1pg5gke xdzw4kq x193iq5w x1xxsxie x7r5mf7 x6ikm8r x10wlt62 xlyipyv xuxw1ft" data-testid="cell-frame-primary-detail"><span class="x140p0ai x1gufx9m x1s928wv xhkezso x1gmr53x x1cpjm7i x1fgarty x1943h6x x193iq5w xeuugli x13faqbe x1vvkbs x1lliihq x1fj9vlw xhslqc4 x1hx0egp x1pg5gke xjb2p0i xo1l8bm xl2ypbo x1ic7a3i" style="--x-fontSize: 12px; --x-lineHeight: 8.5313px; --x-8dd7yt: -0.0137em; --x-hxtmnb: 0.0137em;">Yesterday</span></div></div><div class="x6s0dn4 xhslqc4 x78zum5 x1nxh6w3 x1fc57z9 xr9ek0c xisnujt" data-testid="cell-frame-secondary"><div class="xjbqb8w x1iyjqo2 x1f6kntn x1fc57z9 x6ikm8r x10wlt62 x1yc453h xlyipyv xuxw1ft xo1l8bm"><span class="x78zum5 x1cy8zhl" title="‪SCHOLARSHIP RENEWAL 2026–27**

*Dear Students,*

All students are hereby informed that the *last date for scholarship renewal for the academic year 2026–27 is 5th September 2026*.

All eligible students are advised to complete the scholarship renewal process *without fail before the due date. Students who fail to complete the renewal within the prescribed period will be **responsible for paying their tuition fee*.

For the academic year 2026–27, eligible *SC, ST, BC, EBC, and Minority students* will receive *tuition fee and maintenance fee amounts directly into their bank accounts*.

### *Procedure for Scholarship Renewal*

1. First, students should check whether the *name mentioned in their previous-year Memo and Aadhaar Card is the same. They should also verify their details on the **ePASS website*.

2. If the names are matching, the student must complete *biometric authentication at the nearest MeeSeva centre*.

3. After completing biometric authentication, the student should complete the *renewal application* using the previous year&#39;s Memo. *No other certificates are required.*

4. For this academic year, the *tuition fee will be credited directly to the student&#39;s bank account. Therefore, every student must ensure that their **Aadhaar is seeded with their bank account*. Otherwise, the scholarship amount may not be credited to their account.

5. *For SC Students:* Scholarship renewal is being processed by the *Government SC Welfare Department through the Eligible Applications Auto-Renewal Service. Therefore, SC students **need not  the renewal application separately*.

   However, SC students *must complete biometric authentication at the nearest MeeSeva centre, and  uploaded on the **ePASS website along with the previous year&#39;s Memo. This is **compulsory*.

⚠️ *All eligible students are requested to complete the required process before 15 th September 2026 without fail.*

*Please treat this matter as IMPORTANT and complete the process within the stipulated time.* Important links:
1.SSC memo name &amp; Aadhar name conform: https://tgepass.cgg.gov.in/homeServicePMSSPreRegistrationsRenewal
2. For Renewal applying: https://tgepass.cgg.gov.in/homeServicesPMSRenewalReg
3. Aadhar seeding with Bank AC: https://www.npci.org.in/
4. Application status: https://tgepass.cgg.gov.in/HomeServicePostmatricKnowApplication
5. For SC Students Previous year memo uploading: https://tgepass.cgg.gov.in/homeServicesPmssRenewaluploads‬" data-testid="last-msg-status"><div class="x1c4vz4f x3nfvp2 xuce83p x1bft6iq x1i7k8ik xq9mrsl x6s0dn4"><div class="x78zum5"><span dir="auto" class="x1rg5ohu xnpuxes" style="min-height: 0px;">~Varalakshmi</span></div></div><span>:&nbsp;</span><span dir="ltr" class="x1iyjqo2 x6ikm8r x10wlt62 x1n2onr6 xlyipyv xuxw1ft x1rg5ohu xnpuxes" style="min-height: 0px;">SCHOLARSHIP RENEWAL 2026–27**

*Dear Students,*

All students are hereby informed that the *last date for scholarship renewal for the academic year 2026–27 is 5th September 2026*.

All eligible students are advised to complete the scholarship renewal process *without fail before the due date. Students who fail to complete the renewal within the prescribed period will be **responsible for paying their tuition fee*.

For the academic year 2026–27, eligible *SC, ST, BC, EBC, and Minority students* will receive *tuition fee and maintenance fee amounts directly into their bank accounts*.

### *Procedure for Scholarship Renewal*

1. First, students should check whether the *name mentioned in their previous-year Memo and Aadhaar Card is the same. They should also verify their details on the **ePASS website*.

2. If the names are matching, the student must complete *biometric authentication at the nearest MeeSeva centre*.

3. After completing biometric authentication, the student should complete the *renewal application* using the previous year's Memo. *No other certificates are required.*

4. For this academic year, the *tuition fee will be credited directly to the student's bank account. Therefore, every student must ensure that their **Aadhaar is seeded with their bank account*. Otherwise, the scholarship amount may not be credited to their account.

5. *For SC Students:* Scholarship renewal is being processed by the *Government SC Welfare Department through the Eligible Applications Auto-Renewal Service. Therefore, SC students **need not&nbsp;&nbsp;the renewal application separately*.

&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;However, SC students *must complete biometric authentication at the nearest MeeSeva centre, and&nbsp;&nbsp;uploaded on the **ePASS website along with the previous year's Memo. This is **compulsory*.

